# Copy to .env for local overrides, or set these as real environment
# variables on the deployed host (Railway project → Variables tab).
# Nothing here is required for local dev -- every one of these has a
# working default that assumes a local SQLite database and no vision-LLM
# gateway.

# --- Database -----------------------------------------------------------
# Unset (or absent) = local SQLite at backend/hackathon.db. Set this to a
# real Supabase/Postgres connection string to deploy against Supabase:
#   postgresql://postgres:<password>@<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres
# Get the exact string from Supabase → Project Settings → Database →
# Connection string → URI (use the "Session pooler" string if the direct
# connection is IPv6-only and your host can't reach it).
# DATABASE_URL=

# --- Workstream C5: pothole/crack detector -------------------------------
# Path to the trained weight file (150 MB, git-ignored -- see
# models/README.md). Leave unset locally once you've placed the file at
# models/pothole_best.pt by hand.
# AWAAZIQ_POTHOLE_MODEL=

# A real hosted URL (e.g. a Supabase Storage object URL) the deployed
# server downloads the same file from once, at first use, since a fresh
# deploy has no other way to receive a 150 MB file that isn't in git.
# Local dev doesn't need this if the file is already placed by hand.
# AWAAZIQ_POTHOLE_MODEL_URL=

# --- Workstream C6: building/bridge damage model (prototype-stage) ------
# 1 = on (default), 0 = off. When off, C6 falls back to a lower-confidence
# proxy signal instead of calling a vision-LLM at all.
# AWAAZIQ_VLM_DAMAGE_MODEL=1

# Model slug passed to the omniroute CLI. Only matters when the model
# above is on.
# AWAAZIQ_VLM_MODEL=antigravity/gemini-3.7-flash-medium

# --- OmniRoute gateway (C6's actual call path, prototype/demo only) -----
# These are read by the `omniroute` CLI itself, not by this project's own
# code -- they must be real process environment variables on whatever host
# runs the backend, and the `omniroute` npm package must be installed
# there too (not part of this repo's Python requirements).
#
# This is deliberately NOT meant to run unattended in production: the
# gateway lives on a developer's own machine. To demo C6 on a deployed
# backend, run these locally right before the demo, then set the two
# values below on the deployed host for the duration of the demo:
#   omniroute tunnel create <type>      # exposes localhost:20128 publicly
#   omniroute tokens create             # a real scoped access token
# OMNIROUTE_BASE_URL=
# OMNIROUTE_API_KEY=
